        <h1>Bird's Foot Trefoil</h1>
        <p>Lotus corniculatus</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>

  <div class="container container-spacing" name="main-content">
    <div class="section grid-cards"></div>
  </div>

  <section class="breakout content-image-text">
    <div class="content-image">
      <figure>
        <img class="bg-yellow-100 sm-p-3 shadow-lg" src="/woodland/birds-foot-trefoil.avif" alt="" />
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="content-text species-facts">
      <h4>Species Facts</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Category: </strong>Wildflower</li>
        <li><strong>Scientific name: </strong>Lotus corniculatus</li>
        <li><strong>Height: </strong>up to 35cm</li>
        <li><strong>Status: </strong>Common</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="breakout light-bg">
    <div class="light-bg" name="species-information">
      <div class="section species-information">
        <h2>Species information</h2>
        <div>
          <h4>&nbsp;</h4>
          <h4>Identification</h4>
          <p>
            Its yellow flowers look like little slippers and appear in small clusters. They are followed by seed pods
            that look distinctly like bird's feet or claws, hence the common name. A low-growing plant, its leaves have
            five leaflets and are downy.
          </p>
          <hr />
          <h4>Distribution</h4>
          <p>Widespread</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
